{
  "$comment": "A2A (Agent2Agent) clients of a2a-sdk. A client talks to the agent whose card URL the code gives: `create_client(url)`, `ClientFactory(config).create_from_url(url)` and 0.3's `ClientFactory.connect(url)` fetch the card from `<url>/.well-known/agent-card.json`, `A2ACardResolver(httpx_client, base_url).get_agent_card()` too; `factory.create(card)` takes a card already fetched. The requests go to the interface URL the card lists, which the code does not say: a call keeps the agent's base URL. The 0.3 `A2AClient(httpx_client, url=...)` sends JSON-RPC to its URL. `operation.name` is the A2A 1.0 name of what a method performs; 0.x sends the older method names (`message/send`). Servers (`A2AStarletteApplication`, `A2AFastAPIApplication`, request handlers) receive requests: none of their methods is listed.",
